OL,3,GNEWSABaby charity counts the cost after
OL,4,Abreak-in at HQ
OL,5,
OL,6,FStaff at a charity supporting families
OL,7,Fwith young children living in poverty
OL,8,Fhave said they were left "heartbroken"
OL,9,Fafter discovering their HQ had been
OL,10,Fbroken into.
OL,12,FThe Leeds Baby Bank, in Armley, was
OL,13,Fbelieved to have been raided between
OL,14,FThursday night and Friday morning, with
OL,15,Flaptops, phones and iPads stolen from
OL,16,Fits Wellington Road premises.
OL,18,FThe charity has since launched a
OL,19,Ffundraising campaign to cover the cost
OL,20,Fof the stolen goods, and that had
OL,21,Falready surpassed its original #6,500
OL,22,Ftarget by later on Friday.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,390,380,200,160,0,100
